Dependency archive
------------------
mixxx-deps-2.7-arm64-android-1c20f84a.zip, sha256
6786c09f491166352880984842ffa6f554e974f30a3766a2392298444c1be83c, built from
https://github.com/mixxxdj/vcpkg at 1c20f84aa1ffca2ef18a7d9c6bd7cdd1f5f2e265 (triplet
arm64-android). The recipes and sources of every package below are in that vcpkg
repository and the upstream projects. One file of the archive is replaced by the
build scripts: lib/libportaudio.a is rebuilt from PortAudio b0cc303e with the Mixxx
overlay patches 0001-0004 and our repair 0005 (see tools/android-preview/portaudio/).

The table lists the packages of the archive for arm64-android (generated from the
archive's vcpkg manifest). The APK contains the subset that Mixxx links or loads: the
archive also holds packages that are only used at build time or are not linked into
this app. The licence column is a machine-read hint of the licence texts found in each
package's copyright file (several names mean the file contains several licences, for
example for bundled parts); the authoritative text is the copyright file in the archive
under installed/arm64-android/share/<package>/copyright.

Linked into libmixxx_arm64-v8a.so (checked in the built APK): FFmpeg 7.1 (built with
--enable-libfdk-aac, so the Fraunhofer FDK AAC codec library is statically linked, under
its own licence: see share/fdk-aac/copyright in the archive), TagLib, Rubber Band,
libKeyFinder, FFTW and others of the table. Whether the combination of these licences
allows redistribution of the APK is NOT settled by this file: it is listed as an open
question for the maintainer (fdk-aac with GPL code; libkeyfinder is GPL-3.0 while Mixxx is
GPL-2.0-or-later). The Mixxx project ships the same dependency set in its own Android CI builds.

